~ start
do start_talking()
do disable_movement()
if not Flags.has("blacksmith.quest_offered")
	=> first_meeting
elif Flags.has("blacksmith.axe_given") and not Flags.has("blacksmith.axe_taken")
	=> axe_on_the_ground
elif Flags.has("blacksmith.axe_given")
	=> after
elif not has_rod()
	=> no_rod
elif fish_count() >= fish_price
	=> payday
else
	=> not_enough


#=============================================================================
# The first meeting: the road is shut, he knows the other way, and his price
# is three fish. Ends by setting blacksmith.quest_offered, which is also what
# unlocks the fishing hut's door.
#=============================================================================
~ first_meeting
Blacksmith: HOY! [wait=0.4]Don't just [wave]stand[/wave] there, you'll rust!
Blacksmith: [[Visitor!|A face!|Somebody new!]] Nobody comes here. Nobody comes here and I am delighted about it, which tells you what sort of week I've had.
- I'm trying to get through the land.
	=> road
- I'm just passing through.
	Blacksmith: PASSING THROUGH. Ha! Ha. [wait=0.5]No.
	=> road

~ road
Blacksmith: The old ridge road? Shut. Barricaded. Signed, even, and signs cost money round here, so you know they meant it.
Blacksmith: [shake]Nobody[/shake] goes over the ridge any more.
Blacksmith: [wait=0.6]But there is another way. Oh, there is another way. And exactly one man alive still knows where it starts.
Blacksmith: It's me. I'm the man. [[I'm being modest about it.|That was the modest version.|You can tell I'm the man by the apron.]]
- Will you tell me?
	=> price
- How much?
	Blacksmith: HOW MUCH. He gets it. Look at him, he gets it.
	=> price

~ price
Blacksmith: Three fish.
Blacksmith: [wait=0.5]Three. Fish.
- Fish?
	Blacksmith: Fish! Silver, wriggling, deeply unhelpful about being caught. You've seen fish.
- Three fish for a road?
	Blacksmith: For THE road. And yes. I've eaten nothing but my own bread for eleven days and my own bread is [shake]a punishment[/shake].
Blacksmith: I'd catch them myself, but the river and I have an arrangement: I stay out of it, and it doesn't drown me.
Blacksmith: There's a rod in the old fishing hut up on the north shore. Fellow who lived there hasn't been back in years — he won't begrudge you it.
Blacksmith: Rod. River. Three fish. Then we talk about roads.
do Flags.set_flag("blacksmith.quest_offered")
=> goodbye


#=============================================================================
# Sent for the rod but hasn't got it yet.
#=============================================================================
~ no_rod
Blacksmith: [[Still here? The hut's north. On the shore. Where the water is.|The rod is in the HUT, friend. The hut does not walk to you.|North shore. Old hut. Rod inside. I've made it as small as it goes.]]
Blacksmith: [[No rod, no fish. No fish, no road.|You cannot catch a fish by [wave]glaring[/wave] at it. I have tried.|It's a stick with a string. You'll manage.]]
=> goodbye


#=============================================================================
# Has the rod, hasn't got three fish yet. The rotating heckling, sharpened by
# how close he actually is.
#=============================================================================
~ not_enough
if fish_count() == 0
	Blacksmith: [[Nothing. You've brought me nothing. That's fewer than three, in case you were unsure.|I asked for three fish and you have returned with a damp stick and an expression.|Let me count what you've brought me. [wait=0.6]Done. It was quick.]]
elif fish_count() == 1
	Blacksmith: [[ONE. One is not three! Even the goat knows that and the goat is a disappointment.|A fish! A whole entire fish! And now the other two, which are the ones I asked about.|One down. Two to go. I'll be right here, hitting things.]]
else
	Blacksmith: [[TWO. Agonisingly two. So close I can taste it, and I would very much like to taste it.|Two fish. Two! The third one is out there RIGHT NOW being smug.|One more. ONE. Go and be stern with the river.]]
Blacksmith: [[Off you go.|The river's that way. It hasn't moved.|Shoo. Fish.|Come back heavier.]]
=> goodbye


#=============================================================================
# Payday: takes the three fish, gives up the road, and hands over the axe the
# forest is going to need.
#=============================================================================
~ payday
Blacksmith: [wait=0.4]Is that — [wave]THREE[/wave]?
Blacksmith: Three fish! Three actual fish, in my actual hand! Give them here before one of us changes his mind.
do take_fish()
Blacksmith: [wait=0.8]Beautiful. Ugly. Beautiful and ugly. I'm going to fry all three and I'm not going to share.
Blacksmith: Right. A bargain's a bargain. The way through.
Blacksmith: It's not over the ridge. It's [wave]under[/wave] it. There's a path through the forest — the deep part, the part everyone sensibly avoids — and it comes out the other side of the closed road.
- Through the forest?
	Blacksmith: Through the forest. I know. I know! I said it and I heard it.
- That's it? Just walk in?
	Blacksmith: Just walk in, he says. Just walk in.
Blacksmith: The old path's grown over, and grown over means it's not a path, it's a [shake]hedge with ambitions[/shake]. You'll be cutting your way in.
Blacksmith: Which means you want one of these.
Blacksmith: [wait=1] Here. My spare. It's rusty and the handle's older than you are, but it bites well enough on the small trees.
Blacksmith: [shake]HEADS UP![/shake]
do drop_axe()
do Flags.set_flag("blacksmith.fish_paid")
Blacksmith: [wait=0.5]...I did say heads up.
- You threw an axe at me.
	Blacksmith: I threw an axe [wave]near[/wave] you. There's a whole craft to it.
- My foot.
	Blacksmith: Your foot was in the landing area. That's on the foot.
Blacksmith: Well? Pick it up. It's not going to leap into your hand — [[I have tried.|I've spent hours on that.|Believe me, I've tried.]]
Blacksmith: Once it's in your bag you can swing it with [wave]B[/wave]. Check the bag with "I" if you don't trust me.
Blacksmith: And mind the fragile trees. They come down faster than you'd like and they don't much care where you're standing.
=> goodbye


#=============================================================================
# Thrown, and still lying in the grass where it landed.
#=============================================================================
~ axe_on_the_ground
Blacksmith: [[It's on the ground. Where I threw it. Where it remains.|The axe. Down there. The axe-shaped thing.|I have thrown you an axe and you have elected to stand near it.]]
Blacksmith: [[Bend at the knees.|Pick it [shake]up[/shake].|Grass doesn't need chopping. Trees do. Take the axe.]]
=> goodbye


#=============================================================================
# After the trade.
#=============================================================================
~ after
Blacksmith: [[Still got that axe? Good. Don't bring it back, I've nowhere to put it.|The forest. Cut in, keep going, come out the far side of the road. It's simple, it's just not easy.|Any more fish? [wait=0.7]No? Then we've nothing to discuss, and I say that with enormous affection.]]
Blacksmith: [[Mind the fragile trees.|Watch where they fall.|Don't get clever with the big ones.]]
=> goodbye


~ goodbye
do stop_talking()
do enable_movement()
=> END
